{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486882-m20-technocratic-spheres-paragon","id":1486882,"title":"M20 Technocratic Spheres Paragon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-18T09:30:41-07:00","id":1486882,"title":"M20 Technocratic Spheres Paragon","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I have been looking into the Technocracy optional Spheres, and I was wondering about a potential character that learns all 3 of them (Data, Dimensional Science, Primal Utility).<br /> <br /> In game, as per the M20 Core Book, <b>Dimensional Science</b> and <b>Primal Utiity</b> are related through the theory of <i>Anthropic Principle Fields</i>, so it does not seem inconceivable that a Technocrat could learn both. <b>Data</b> is more limited, but it is taught outside the NWO.<br /> <br /> Based on that, long time ago, I made a post on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290499-technocratic-spheres-learning-restrictions\">who could learn those spheres</a>, but assuming that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a>\u00b4s <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290499-technocratic-spheres-learning-restrictions?p=1290707#post1290707\">post</a> there is feasible, I have some questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Is there any advantage on learning all 3 Spheres?</b> <i>I only see an even stronger dependency on Technology for them to work.</i></li> <li><b>How would the Technocracy react to a member learning all three? </b><i>I would think that this person would be a bit odd in a good way, perhaps mending bridges among the Factions.</i></li> <li><b>How would the Technocracy react to an Orphan learning all three of them outside Technocracy tutelage? </b><i>I would think that they would be close to overjoyed as random reality deviants start aligning on their own with the consensus the Technocracy wants.</i></li> <li><b>Regarding the Psionics practice, would it work will all three Spheres? </b><i>I think it would work, but I rather have confirmation.</i></li> <li><b>IF the answer to question 4 is yes, can Psionics and a high enough Arete / Enlightenment allow you to work without technical devices?</b></li> <li><b>IF the answer to question 5 is yes, how does this impact Data limits?</b></li> <li><b>Is there any way for Data to work without technological devices (both on the user and the recipient)?</b><i> Something like high enough Arete / Enlightenment</i></li> </ol>Thanks for the time invested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 08-02-2022, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T10:25:19-07:00","id":1486886,"title":"","content":"Consider the Psychic Phenomena of Cyberkinesis and Cyberpathy for examples of how the concepts inherent in Data can be expressed through the Psionic Practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T11:36:34-07:00","id":1486891,"title":"","content":"1.<br /> Being dependant on technology shouldn't be a big problem for a typical Technocrat (if you are dependant, I take note that many questions are about how not to be). You will see loads of it. Now, you would be no Space Marine taming wyld Realms - with the risk of being &quot;lost in space&quot; or having to survive with your body and the surroundings as only tools - but as long as you keep close to the resources of the Technocracy there would be no problem.<br /> <br /> Some ideas:<br /> *It would make a pretty good kit for a very specialist kind of Digital Web explorer that wants to ger *into* it, holistically, and explore it's connections to other Realms. It would allow to vigil the interactions between the big data, and both the humane and supernatural forces that interact with it.<br /> <br /> *It would make a good assessor to the economy and potential of off-world colonies, being able to investigate better than anyone else the unconventional assets that can be found out there, and create networks to better exploit or improve on these conditions.<br /> <br /> For me it's reminiscent of the Anime <i>Martian Successor Nadesico</i>, where there was an accountant on a spaceship because the ship belonged to a private corporation...not that VE really work that way, but I wouldn't think too terrible a stretch to find as inspiration.<br /> <br /> 2.<br /> It would be odd. If that's good or bad would depend somehwat on the &quot;setting&quot; of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Being the one in the middle on an age of tension usually means that everyone fears and/or hates you. In the era of the potential civil war PU and Data belong to factions that aren't on the best of terms, but the real problem here it's DS because a non-VE with DS (and Data!) could enter in contact with things that nobody else it's supposed to know.<br /> <br /> In more prosperous ages, I see knowledge flowing more amenably<br /> <br /> 3.<br /> Orphans are still Deviants. They're going to be overjoyed if the Orphan joins. Technocrats will hardly be &quot;overjoyed&quot; by Orphans that refuse to toe to the line. They're being Unmutual.<br /> <br /> There are other concerns that, I think, would condition their attitude more. Like, if the Orphan does a lot of Vulgar stuff (Paradox it's against the law), or how it's using his knowledge, and if the Orphan uses<i> Practices and Instruments </i>aproved by the Technocracy. Perhaps &quot;letting live&quot; it's how Technocrats express &quot;joy&quot; about the choices of a Deviant :P<br /> <br /> Learning these spheres ins't any guarantee that their <i>Focus </i>it's going to be &quot;the rigth one&quot;. That's much more important than the Sphere<br /> <br /> 4.<br /> Like, they could learn Psionics, which it's not terrible but very fringe - almost to the point of ethertech. AFAIK, Psionics &quot;overcringe&quot; more than &quot;overjoy&quot; rigth-minded Technocrats :P<br /> <br /> But yes, there's no hard rule to say it won't. After all you just need a good justification. Psionics it's a very pop-culture &quot;wish uppon a star&quot; kind of thing. If <i>Technopathy </i>exists, I see not why a psion couldn't be connected to dimensional anomalies, to a world made of all the Information of the universe, to market fluctuations and notions of value...<br /> <br /> I would demand a real explanation, telling how your powers work more in depth, tough.<br /> <br /> 5.<br /> As per M20, Technocrats are Conditioned to never be able to work without Instruments, if that's what you're talking about.<br /> <br /> I would allow for Psionics to be used as a Mystic Focus for scientific minded mages (I would also allow several forms of &quot;superstitionist&quot; crafts as Technomancy, too - provided it has an advantage instead of just being a penalization of your style), and drop it's Instruments like that. But, RAW, that's not the case.<br /> <br /> If you're talking about the Spheres needing devices. Well, do they?. I didn't know they did, but if they do obviously it goes beyond what Focus can do. I tought only Data really did had such a limitation, and only insofar as it was limited to work where there's some form of communication network (from Internet to the telegraph) - which I found as an unusual and harsh limitation.<br /> <br /> I don't see why you should need anything but your Instruments - the fact you even need them it's <i>already </i>a penalty on your Technomancer.<br /> <br /> 6.<br /> Not that I know.<br /> <br /> Well, with potent enough magick you make make sure there's *always* Signal :P - the Internet goes wherever you go :P<br /> <br /> Albeit, as said, I think that as a harsh and unusual limitation - there's &quot;information&quot; and &quot;relations&quot; everywhere, ask any Virtual Adept. And even if human intervention was needed, for some Paradigmatic reason, why isn't &quot;a map&quot;, &quot;a book with information&quot;, etc... enough of a data-source for it to work - I would think those more relevant data to, say, an Effect made to unerringly find someone in an area, than &quot;a telegraph&quot; passing trough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-18-2022, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T05:03:20-07:00","id":1487365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486882-m20-technocratic-spheres-paragon#post1486882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> I have some questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Is there any advantage on learning all 3 Spheres?</b> <i>I only see an even stronger dependency on Technology for them to work.</i></li> <li><b>How would the Technocracy react to a member learning all three? </b><i>I would think that this person would be a bit odd in a good way, perhaps mending bridges among the Factions.</i></li> </ol>Thanks for the time invested.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any advantages a Mage would get from learning three similarily themed kinds of Magick / Technomancy should be in line with what would you think a particularly talented Tradition (or Nephandi) Mage would get if she or he would study hard enough to learn Sphere variants or Rotes close in-line with her or his Tradition or more minor group. She should definitely get some sort of benefit, even if indirect one like easier increase in some Attributes or Backgrounds, or access to Rotes which require Conjunctional use of these Technocratic Sphere variants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T08:35:37-07:00","id":1487384,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3254_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3254\" data-vbnamecard=\"3254\">Muad'Dib</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> for your answers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},